  "published": "2026-11-09T04:09:40.067Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.3.0: Client IP input normalized (IPv4-mapped IPv6 in any spelling, a.b.c.d:port, [..]:port, surrounding whitespace); stricter dotted-quad parsing; private, reserved and documentation IPv4 ranges return NotFound without a database call. LookupAsync(ip, fields, CancellationToken) on GeoIp, GeoIpClient and IGeoIpLookup; synchronous Lookup marked [Obsolete]. GeoIpOptions / GeoIpClient / IGeoIpLookup: connection string or connection factory supplied by the host (binds from IConfiguration), configurable command timeout; GeoIp.Configure(options); GeoIpSchema.EnsureCreated(GeoIpOptions).\n      v1.2.2: Lookup query rewritten as a backward index seek (4 logical reads instead of up to ~50k pages / 300 ms for high IPs). No API or schema change.\n      v1.2.1: Added README to package.\n      v1.2.0: Migrated to .NET 10. Switched to Microsoft.Data.SqlClient and System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager NuGet packages.\n      v1.1.0: Added GeoIpSchema.EnsureCreated() and EnsureCreated(connectionString) overload.\n      v1.0.0: Initial release with GeoIp.Lookup(), IpLocation, LocationField.",
